Obviously, $\ds{\color{#00f}{\large c = {1 \over 5}}}$: 

 \begin{align}
&\color{#00f}{\large%
\ell = \lim_{x \to \infty}\bracks{\pars{x^{5} + 7x^{4} + 2}^{1/5} - x}}
=\lim_{x \to \infty}\braces{%
x\bracks{\pars{1 + {7 \over x} + {2 \over x^{5}}}^{1/5} - 1}}
\\[3mm]&=\lim_{x \to \infty}\pars{%
x\braces{\bracks{1 + {1 \over 5}\pars{{7 \over x} + {2 \over x^{5}}}} - 1}}
=\lim_{x \to \infty}\braces{%
x\bracks{{1 \over 5}\pars{{7 \over x} + {2 \over x^{5}}}}}
=\color{#00f}{\large{7 \over 5}}
\end{align} 

 $$
\color{#00f}{\large{\ell - 2c}} = {7 \over 5} - 2\pars{1 \over 5} =
\color{#00f}{\Large 1}
